{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-74615","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105922","text":"Skill 01 — The Ten Protocols"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74617","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105923","text":"OS-001 through OS-010: what each protocol specifies, which product implements it, and the cognitive science behind it. Eight cognitive primitives plus two cross-cutting protocols (PRISM diagnostic, PULSE temporal)."}]}],"id":"blk-74616","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-74618","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105924","text":"Overview"}]},{"id":"blk-74619","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105925","text":"OpenSentience publishes ten numbered protocols organized in two layers:"}]},{"id":"blk-74620","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74622","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105926","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive primitives (OS-001 — OS-008)"},{"id":"spn-105927","text":" — eight individual capabilities,"}]}],"id":"blk-74621","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74623","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105928","text":"each grounded in a cognitive science thread."}]},{"id":"blk-74624","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74626","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105929","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cross-cutting protocols (OS-009 PRISM, OS-010 PULSE)"},{"id":"spn-105930","text":" — two sibling"}]}],"id":"blk-74625","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74627","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105931","text":"protocols that sit above the cognitive primitives and above the [&] structural composition layer. PULSE declares how every loop in the ecosystem cycles, nests, and signals; PRISM measures how well those loops actually learn over time."}]},{"id":"blk-74628","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105932","text":"The protocols are independent specifications — they can be adopted individually or composed together. A system may publish a PULSE manifest without implementing any cognitive primitive, and PRISM can benchmark any PULSE-conforming system without bespoke per-system integration."}]},{"id":"blk-74629","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105933","text":"OS-001: Continual Learning"}]},{"id":"blk-74630","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105934","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-105935","text":" Hippocampal consolidation (McClelland et al. 1995)"}]},{"id":"blk-74631","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105936","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74632","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74634","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105937","text":"Three node types: episodic (events), semantic (facts), procedural (workflows)"}]}],"id":"blk-74633","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74636","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105938","text":"Typed, weighted edges between nodes"}]}],"id":"blk-74635","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74638","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105939","text":"Confidence scores with evidence-calibrated assignment"}]}],"id":"blk-74637","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74640","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105940","text":"Consolidation cycle: decay low-confidence nodes, prune stale entries,"}]}],"id":"blk-74639","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74641","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105941","text":"merge near-duplicates, strengthen co-retrieved edges"}]},{"id":"blk-74642","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74644","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105942","text":"Memory timescales: working memory (session), short-term (hours), long-term"}]}],"id":"blk-74643","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74645","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105943","text":"(persistent)"}]},{"id":"blk-74646","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105944","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-105945","text":" New memories must be stored quickly (hippocampal fast-write) without disrupting existing knowledge (neocortical slow-consolidation). This maps to immediate ETS/SQLite writes with background consolidation."}]},{"id":"blk-74647","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105946","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-105947","text":" Graphonomous ("},{"id":"spn-105948","marks":["code"],"text":"store_node"},{"id":"spn-105949","text":", "},{"id":"spn-105950","marks":["code"],"text":"store_edge"},{"id":"spn-105951","text":", "},{"id":"spn-105952","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-105953","text":", "},{"id":"spn-105954","marks":["code"],"text":"run_consolidation"},{"id":"spn-105955","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-74648","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105956","text":"OS-002: Topological Routing (kappa)"}]},{"id":"blk-74649","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105957","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-105958","text":" Working memory gating (O'Reilly & Frank 2006)"}]},{"id":"blk-74650","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105959","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74651","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74653","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105960","text":"The kappa parameter: a measure of cyclicity in a knowledge subgraph"}]}],"id":"blk-74652","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74655","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105961","text":"Strongly connected component (SCC) detection on retrieved neighborhoods"}]}],"id":"blk-74654","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74657","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105962","text":"Routing decision: kappa = 0 implies fast path (acyclic, no conflict),"}]}],"id":"blk-74656","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74658","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105963","text":"kappa > 0 implies deliberate path (cycles exist, may contain contradictions)"}]},{"id":"blk-74659","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74661","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105964","text":"Topological features: SCC count, max SCC size, edge density within cycles"}]}],"id":"blk-74660","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74662","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105965","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-105966","text":" The prefrontal cortex gates information into working memory based on relevance and conflict signals. Kappa serves as the conflict signal — cyclic knowledge regions indicate unresolved tension that requires deliberation before action."}]},{"id":"blk-74663","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105967","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-105968","text":" Graphonomous routing layer ("},{"id":"spn-105969","marks":["code"],"text":"topology_analyze"},{"id":"spn-105970","text":", "},{"id":"spn-105971","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-105972","text":" topology annotations)"}]},{"id":"blk-74664","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105973","text":"OS-003: Deliberation Orchestrator"}]},{"id":"blk-74665","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105974","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-105975","text":" Dual-process theory (Kahneman 2011)"}]},{"id":"blk-74666","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105976","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74667","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74669","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105977","text":"Four-phase deliberation: bid, debate, vote, commit"}]}],"id":"blk-74668","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74671","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105978","text":"Argumentation framework: claims, warrants, rebuttals"}]}],"id":"blk-74670","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74673","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105979","text":"Consensus mechanisms: majority, supermajority, unanimity"}]}],"id":"blk-74672","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74675","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105980","text":"Timeout and escalation policies"}]}],"id":"blk-74674","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74677","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105981","text":"Triggered when kappa routing indicates deliberation is needed"}]}],"id":"blk-74676","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74678","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105982","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-105983","text":" System 1 (fast, automatic) handles routine decisions. System 2 (slow, deliberate) engages when conflict is detected. The kappa threshold is the trigger that shifts from fast to deliberate processing."}]},{"id":"blk-74679","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105984","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-105985","text":" AgenTroMatic ("},{"id":"spn-105986","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberate"},{"id":"spn-105987","text":" tool in Graphonomous provides the single-agent deliberation path)"}]},{"id":"blk-74680","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105988","text":"OS-004: Attention Engine"}]},{"id":"blk-74681","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105989","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-105990","text":" Endogenous attention (Desimone & Duncan 1995)"}]},{"id":"blk-74682","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105991","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74683","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74685","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105992","text":"Three-phase cycle: survey (scan environment), triage (rank by salience),"}]}],"id":"blk-74684","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74686","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105993","text":"dispatch (act on highest-priority items)"}]},{"id":"blk-74687","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74689","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105994","text":"Salience scoring: combines urgency, recency, goal relevance, and confidence"}]}],"id":"blk-74688","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74691","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105995","text":"Goal bias: active goals increase salience of related knowledge"}]}],"id":"blk-74690","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74693","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105996","text":"Dispatch modes: act (execute), learn (gather more context), escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-74692","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74694","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105997","text":"(request human intervention), idle (nothing needed)"}]},{"id":"blk-74695","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105998","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-105999","text":" Biological attention is goal-directed (endogenous) not just stimulus-driven (exogenous). The attention engine prioritizes based on the agent's active goals, not just what is new or loud."}]},{"id":"blk-74696","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106000","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106001","text":" Graphonomous attention module ("},{"id":"spn-106002","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_survey"},{"id":"spn-106003","text":", "},{"id":"spn-106004","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_run_cycle"},{"id":"spn-106005","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-74697","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106006","text":"OS-005: Model Tier Adaptation"}]},{"id":"blk-74698","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106007","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106008","text":" Resource rationality (Lieder & Griffiths 2020)"}]},{"id":"blk-74699","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106009","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74700","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74702","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106010","text":"Three tiers: "},{"id":"spn-106011","marks":["code"],"text":"local_small"},{"id":"spn-106012","text":" (8B parameter models), "},{"id":"spn-106013","marks":["code"],"text":"local_large"},{"id":"spn-106014","text":" (70B+),"}]}],"id":"blk-74701","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74703","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106015","marks":["code"],"text":"cloud_frontier"},{"id":"spn-106016","text":" (largest available)"}]},{"id":"blk-74704","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74706","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106017","text":"Same topology and tool surface at every tier — only depth and latency differ"}]}],"id":"blk-74705","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74708","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106018","text":"Escalation rules: when local_small confidence is below threshold, escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-74707","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74709","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106019","text":"to local_large; when local_large is insufficient, escalate to cloud_frontier"}]},{"id":"blk-74710","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74712","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106020","text":"Budget constraints: token limits, latency targets, cost caps per tier"}]}],"id":"blk-74711","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74713","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106021","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-106022","text":" Optimal cognition allocates computational resources proportional to decision importance. Simple decisions use fast/cheap processing; high-stakes decisions justify expensive computation."}]},{"id":"blk-74714","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106023","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106024","text":" Graphonomous and Agentelic (tier selection and escalation logic)"}]},{"id":"blk-74715","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106025","text":"OS-006: Agent Governance Shim"}]},{"id":"blk-74716","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106026","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106027","text":" Executive function (Miyake et al. 2000)"}]},{"id":"blk-74717","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106028","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74718","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74720","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106029","text":"Permission taxonomy: filesystem, network, tool_invocation, graph_access"}]}],"id":"blk-74719","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74722","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106030","text":"Lifecycle state machine: installed, enabled, running, disabled, removed"}]}],"id":"blk-74721","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74724","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106031","text":"Graduated autonomy: observe, advise, act"}]}],"id":"blk-74723","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74726","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106032","text":"Append-only audit trail with typed events"}]}],"id":"blk-74725","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74728","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106033","text":"OTP-native implementation: GenStateMachine, ETS, DynamicSupervisor"}]}],"id":"blk-74727","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74729","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106034","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-106035","text":" Executive function provides inhibitory control (permissions), task switching (lifecycle), and cognitive flexibility (autonomy levels). Without executive function, an agent cannot self-regulate — it either does nothing or does everything."}]},{"id":"blk-74730","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106036","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106037","text":" "},{"id":"spn-106038","marks":["code"],"text":"open_sentience"},{"id":"spn-106039","text":" hex package (this project)"}]},{"id":"blk-74731","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106040","text":"OS-007: Adversarial Robustness"}]},{"id":"blk-74732","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106041","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106042","text":" Immune system — self/non-self discrimination"}]},{"id":"blk-74733","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106043","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74734","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74736","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106044","text":"Five threat categories: prompt injection, model poisoning, side-channel,"}]}],"id":"blk-74735","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74737","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106045","text":"identity spoofing, resource exhaustion"}]},{"id":"blk-74738","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74740","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106046","text":"Detection rules per category"}]}],"id":"blk-74739","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74742","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106047","text":"Defense protocols: quarantine, circuit-break, escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-74741","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74744","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106048","text":"Integration with OS-006 for permission revocation and OS-008 for circuit"}]}],"id":"blk-74743","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74745","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106049","text":"breaking"}]},{"id":"blk-74746","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106050","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106051","text":" OpenSentience security module (draft)"}]},{"id":"blk-74747","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106052","text":"OS-008: Agent Harness"}]},{"id":"blk-74748","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106053","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106054","text":" Supervisory attentional system (Norman & Shallice 1986)"}]},{"id":"blk-74749","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106055","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74750","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74752","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106056","text":"Pipeline ordering enforcement (retrieve → route → act → learn)"}]}],"id":"blk-74751","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74754","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106057","text":"Quality gates between pipeline stages"}]}],"id":"blk-74753","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74756","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106058","text":"Sprint contracts: bounded execution with explicit goals and success criteria"}]}],"id":"blk-74755","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74758","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106059","text":"Context management: 60% threshold, compaction, Graphonomous overflow"}]}],"id":"blk-74757","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74760","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106060","text":"Generator-evaluator separation for adversarial grading"}]}],"id":"blk-74759","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74761","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106061","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106062","text":" OpenSentience harness module (draft)"}]},{"id":"blk-74762","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106063","text":"OS-009: PRISM — Protocol for Rating Iterative System Memory"}]},{"id":"blk-74763","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106064","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106065","text":" Meta-cognition + psychometrics (Item Response Theory, signal detection theory)"}]},{"id":"blk-74764","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106066","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74765","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74767","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106067","text":"9 continual-learning dimensions (retention, plasticity, transfer,"}]}],"id":"blk-74766","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74768","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106068","text":"contradiction handling, etc.)"}]},{"id":"blk-74769","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74771","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106069","text":"4-phase evaluation loop: compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose"}]}],"id